  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S3 ;
  triage:title "New AI.23 adapter-side-effect boundary gate uses gameable substring matching instead of AST-based enforcement" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs::ai23_write_ingress_has_one_http_resource_and_no_adapter_side_effects enforces its forbidden-call list via raw substring matching against literal tokens instead of AST-based enforcement. This is trivially defeated by differently-named private helpers that duplicate logic without matching the forbidden tokens. The same file already contains HostRoutingVisitor with alias/binding resolution (lines 310-616) for AI.12, which was not extended to this new check despite AI.23 sub-task 2 requiring fail-closed enforcement." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
